hypotheses.statement:
Let $U$ be a smooth connected affine complex variety of dimension $n\ge1$. Let $F$ be a holomorphic line bundle on $U$ with a smooth semipositive metric of weight $S$, let $g$ be a global plurisubharmonic function not identically $-\infty$, and let $s$ be a holomorphic $F$-valued $(n,0)$-form. Fix $R\in\mathbb R$, a smooth cutoff $0\le\chi\le1$ equal to one for $t\le-R-1$ and zero for $t\ge-R$, and a smooth convex function $f$ that is affine of positive slope $c$ near $-\infty$, with $c\le f'\le d$ for some $d$ and $f''>0$ on $[-R-1,-R]$. If $$M=\int_{\{g<-R\}}|s|^2e^{-S}<\infty,$$ there is a measurable $F$-valued top form $u$ such that $$\label{mm:eq:localization-estimate}
 \bar\partial u=\bar\partial(\chi(g)s),\qquad
 \int_U|u|^2e^{-S-f(g)}\le C_{\chi,f}M,$$ where the equation is distributional and $$\label{mm:eq:localization-constant}
 C_{\chi,f}=\max_{[-R-1,-R]}
 \frac{|\chi'|^2e^{-f}}{f''}.$$ The constant is independent of $U,F,S,g,s$ and of the auxiliary complete Kähler metrics. At $g=-\infty$ we set $\chi(g)=1$ and $f(g)=-\infty$; that locus has measure zero.

